  ('93fd51ad-f177-4f47-87ea-3d0c6b701821','Dewitt Archery Team, listed in Michigan''s Dewitt area, appears in the IBO directory as a pro shop, connecting it to the International Bowhunting Organization''s network of retailers and 3D shooting resources rather than a standalone unaffiliated business. Central Michigan has a solid bowhunting following, and an IBO-listed shop typically serves archers looking for equipment tied into that organization''s 3D competition circuit, alongside general sales and service. The team name suggests a competitive shooting group associated with the shop beyond pure retail, though that isn''t spelled out further in the record. Anyone interested in visiting or shooting with the team should contact the shop directly.'),
  ('3374dc14-e24b-4949-91fa-592e9cf161bd','Dinosaur Valley Archery Club takes its name from the Glen Rose, Texas area''s famous dinosaur track fossils, and runs as an ASA-affiliated 3D archery club putting it on the same national circuit as other Archery Shooters Association groups across the state. This part of North Texas, along the Paluxy River, has enough wooded and hilly terrain to support a realistic 3D course, appealing to local bowhunters working on shot placement ahead of season. ASA affiliation generally signals a scored, animal-target format rather than standard bullseye shooting. Randy Duren is listed as the club''s contact, a solid first call for questions about upcoming shoots.'),
  ('d41b197a-f824-4d07-8882-62cf90a53104','Dixon Range, a volunteer club in Clintwood, Virginia, deep in the state''s coalfield region near the Kentucky border, holds ASA affiliation and runs a 3D archery course for its members. Southwest Virginia''s steep, wooded terrain makes for a demanding and realistic 3D layout, well suited to bowhunters sharpening their skills on animal targets before deer season in this heavily forested part of Appalachia. Being ASA-affiliated ties the club into the broader Archery Shooters Association competition circuit, giving members a chance to shoot scored rounds beyond informal practice. Bobby Mullins is listed as the contact, worth reaching out to for shoot dates and course access.'),
  ('039a3163-15b8-4e60-8db2-a1b9cf25667a','Eastman, Georgia''s Dodge County Team Bullseyes shows up in the IBO pro shop directory, a signal of its ties to bowhunting and 3D archery culture in this part of central Georgia. As a commercial range, it caters to walk-in shooters looking to tune a setup or spend an afternoon on the line rather than committing to club membership. Dodge County sits in serious deer-hunting country, and a range with IBO recognition often draws archers prepping bows for hunting season alongside target shooters. Specific hours, lane counts, and pricing aren''t listed here, so archers heading to Eastman should call or check with Dodge County Team Bullseyes directly before making the drive.'),
  ('0516c9dd-0625-4d3f-a56b-8229ab78912e','Downwind Nockbusters in Idaho Falls, Idaho is a USA Archery affiliated club running an unusually broad set of programs: Junior Olympic Archery Development for young shooters, an Adult Archery Program, and both 3D and field archery for members who want a target game that mimics hunting terrain and distance judgment. Idaho Falls sits in a region where bowhunting and target sport overlap heavily, and a club offering JOAD alongside 3D and field rounds serves that crossover well, letting archers move between disciplines without switching organizations. Anyone in eastern Idaho looking to get a kid into competitive archery, or add 3D rounds to their own practice, should reach out to Downwind Nockbusters for current schedules and enrollment details.'),
  ('47783923-5412-4097-a0dc-47f40ad246c6','Drawn to Him is an ASA-affiliated 3D archery club based in Selma, North Carolina, run by volunteers rather than paid staff, typical of the ASA model across the state. The 3D format means shooting foam animal targets at marked or unmarked distances through a wooded course, closely mirroring real bowhunting shots, and ASA affiliation usually points to organized shoots tied into the broader 3D competition circuit. Chris Willard is listed as the club''s contact, a good starting point for anyone wanting to visit or ask about joining. Central North Carolina has a solid bowhunting culture, and a volunteer-run 3D club like this fits naturally into that scene. Reach out directly for shoot dates and access details.'),
  ('f56eb868-81c2-40ac-8986-c4b1e884aeb9','Dream Chasers JOAD is a USA Archery affiliated club in Payson, Arizona focused specifically on the Junior Olympic Archery Development pathway, the national program that trains young archers through structured levels toward competitive shooting. Payson sits up in Mogollon Rim country, a couple hours from Phoenix, and a dedicated JOAD program gives families in that area a real option for youth archery instruction without a long drive into the valley. Unlike clubs that run multiple program tracks, Dream Chasers appears centered on the JOAD pipeline itself, which can mean more focused coaching attention for kids working through the ranks. Parents interested in enrolling a young archer should contact Dream Chasers JOAD directly for age requirements, schedules, and costs.'),
  ('f9ba8dff-3d19-4af4-bfdd-e6820a81b01d','DropTine 3D Archery is an ASA-affiliated 3D club in Morehead, Kentucky, run by volunteers and built around the foam-animal target format ASA is known for. Eastern Kentucky has deep bowhunting roots, and a 3D club gives local hunters a way to practice realistic shot angles and distance estimation outside of hunting season. Chris Rowley is listed as the club''s contact, the right person to reach out to about shoot schedules or joining. As with most volunteer-run clubs, access and course availability likely depend on member involvement rather than fixed public hours. Anyone near Morehead interested in 3D archery should contact DropTine 3D Archery directly to confirm when the course is open.'),
  ('508072c5-7aef-47f4-9a81-ff1598221d95','Duncan Bowhunters is a volunteer-run, ASA-affiliated 3D archery club in Duncan, Oklahoma, southwest of Oklahoma City in classic Oklahoma bowhunting country. The ASA affiliation points to a 3D foam-target course, built to simulate real hunting shots at varying, often unmarked distances. Debbie Dulworth is the listed contact, a useful first call for anyone wanting to check shoot dates or ask about joining as a member. Volunteer clubs like this one typically run around scheduled shoot days rather than set public hours, so showing up unannounced isn''t the best approach. Archers or bowhunters near Duncan looking to sharpen shot placement before deer season should reach out directly to find out what''s currently running.'),
  ('4a932930-7217-4bd2-a116-b9491501b5b1','Dyke Springs Archery Club is a volunteer-run, ASA-affiliated 3D archery club in Hope, Arkansas, in the southwestern part of the state. Like other ASA clubs, it''s organized around a foam-animal 3D course meant to mimic real bowhunting shots at varying distances, a format that draws hunters looking to stay sharp between seasons. Nick Hammond is the listed contact, the person to reach out to for shoot days, course access, or membership. Being volunteer-run, the club likely doesn''t keep fixed public hours, operating instead around scheduled shoots and member availability. Southwestern Arkansas has a strong hunting tradition, and clubs like this one give local archers organized structure a solo backyard setup can''t match.'),
  ('590f1000-13ba-4667-9462-01d7c22db544','E and J Archery shows up in the IBO pro shop directory, putting this commercial operation in West Hampton, Massachusetts on the map for bowhunters connected to the International Bowhunting Organization''s competition circuit. Western Massachusetts has a real hunting culture, and a pro shop with IBO recognition tends to draw archers who take bow tuning and 3D competition seriously rather than casual walk-ins alone. As a commercial range, E and J Archery likely doesn''t require membership, though specific hours, lane counts, and services beyond the pro shop aren''t detailed in the available data. Archers in the area looking to get equipment serviced or find local 3D shoot information should contact E and J Archery directly to confirm what''s currently offered.'),
  ('d5dbf45b-c468-4090-b257-0aa4e46a8d0e','Eagle Archers in Blountville, Tennessee is a USA Archery affiliated club running both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program for kids and an Adult Archery Program for grown members, giving a whole family a path into the sport under one club. Blountville sits in the Tri-Cities region of northeast Tennessee, and JOAD in particular has become a common on-ramp for kids who might otherwise never pick up a recurve or compound bow. Running both youth and adult tracks together suggests a club built for multi-generational participation rather than one narrow age group. Families in the Tri-Cities area interested in structured archery instruction should reach out to Eagle Archers directly for enrollment details and current schedules.'),
  ('1388fada-58fe-4a16-9acd-ca1fde1e8d3d','Eagle Creek Archery in Statesboro, Georgia is a USA Archery affiliated club offering both Junior Olympic Archery Development for young shooters and an Adult Archery Program for older members, letting a whole household get involved through the same club. Statesboro is home to Georgia Southern University, and a college town setting often brings a mix of families and students looking for a structured, coached activity outside the usual sports options. JOAD''s step-by-step curriculum tends to appeal to parents wanting real instruction rather than just handing a kid a bow, and an adult track alongside it means the club isn''t only built around youth. Anyone in the Statesboro area should contact Eagle Creek Archery directly for enrollment and schedule information.'),
  ('5065415b-ec06-4413-a3f6-9ae93ab9ef6b','Eagle Outdoors Archery Club is a volunteer-run, ASA-affiliated 3D club in Neosho, Missouri, in the southwestern corner of the state near the Arkansas and Oklahoma borders. The ASA tie means a foam-animal course designed to mirror real bowhunting shots, popular with hunters using the off-season to sharpen distance judgment and shot placement. Jeremy Whittle is listed as the contact, the right person to reach for shoot schedules or membership questions. This corner of Missouri has a strong deer-hunting culture, and a volunteer 3D club fits that scene naturally, running on member participation rather than fixed public hours. Anyone interested in joining should contact Eagle Outdoors Archery Club directly to find out when the course is active.'),
  ('abe3ad40-601b-402c-8031-9ced26169688','East Alabama Archery Association is a volunteer-run, ASA-affiliated 3D club based in Opelika, Alabama, just outside Auburn. The ASA connection points to a foam-animal 3D course built for practicing realistic hunting shots at varying distances, a format that draws serious bowhunters as much as target shooters. Don Jackson is the listed contact for the association, worth reaching out to for shoot dates or membership terms. East Alabama''s rural surroundings and hunting culture make a volunteer 3D club a natural fit here, and the Auburn area''s population brings a steady stream of potential members even though the club runs on volunteer effort rather than paid staff. Anyone near Opelika interested in 3D archery should contact the association directly.')
) AS v(id, description)
WHERE r.id = v.id::uuid AND r.is_claimed = false;
